==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|bot}}

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|enm|bōte|t=advantage, benefit, profit; relief, salvation; atonement, amends, expiation; cure}}, from {{der|en|ang|bōt|t=help, relief, advantage, remedy; compensation for an injury or wrong; (peace) offering, recompense, amends, atonement, reformation, penance, repentance}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bōtō|t=recompense}}. {{doublet|en|boot}} (inherited from the same {{m+|enm|-}} word).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/bəʊt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/boʊt/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s}} {{lb|en|legal|historical}}

# The [[atonement]], [[compensation]], [[amends]], [[satisfaction]]; as, [[manbote]], a compensation for a man slain.
# A [[privilege]] or [[allowance]] of necessaries, especially in [[feudal]] times.
# A right to take wood from property not one's own.

====Usage notes====
* Often used to form compounds indicating a right to take wood only for a specific purpose.

