==Middle English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|enm|ang|bōt}}, from {{inh|enm|gem-pro|*bōtō}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|enm|boot|bot|boote}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|enm|/boːt/}}

====Noun====
{{enm-noun|botes|pl2=boten}}

# {{senseid|enm|help}} Help, [[advantage]], benefit; that which is [[good]], [[helpful]], or relieving:
#*: ''Heo lufeden bi wurten, bi moren, and bi rote; nas þer nan oðer '''boten'''.'' &mdash; Layamon's Brut, 1275
## Saving or [[extrication]] from [[distress]] or [[danger]]; something or someone which provides it.
## Salvation {{gloss|release or rescue from eternal punishment}}, or one who acts as salvation
## An avenue of [[escape]]; a method through which one can release [[themself]] from danger.
## Utility, usefulness; that which is [[useful]], [[expedient]], or [[suitable]].
## A [[reprieve]] or the offering of [[forgiveness]] from punishment or danger.
# Activity done as [[redress]] or [[recompense]] for (one's or another's) sins; [[expiation]].
#*: ''Iesu {{...}} For synne þat hath my soule bounde, Let þi blessed blood be my '''bote'''.'' &mdash; Iesu þat art hevene
# [[mirth|Mirth]], [[gladness]]; the feeling or emotion of being [[happy]] and [[joyful]].
# The [[quelling]], [[curing]], or [[expurgation]] of disease or sickness; medical recovery.
# {{lb|enm|rare}} Recompense, [[amends]] or compensation; behaviour in return for one's wrongs.
# {{lb|enm|rare}} An [[extra]], [[augment]], or [[addition]]; something [[to boot]].
# {{lb|enm|rare}} A medicinal or pharmaceutical [[cure]] or [[remedy]]; something used to quell disease.
# {{lb|enm|rare}} Repair work; the act of fixing structures or buildings.
#*: ''Þey shulde..do '''bote''' to brugges þat to-broke were.'' &mdash; Pier's Plowman, 1400

